# tests/web_snapshots/VERSION — READ THIS FILE before touching any baseline
# PNG in this directory. It is the stable, mandatory-read RULES document for
# the committed screenshots. The per-event regeneration record (which
# baseline(s) changed, why, and how it was verified) is NOT appended here —
# it lives one file per event under tests/web_snapshots/history/, so two
# branches regenerating different baselines never write the same file. See
# "RULE 3" below and tests/web_snapshots/history/README.md.
#
# RULE 1 — the pins. `playwright install` pins the browser build PER
# PLAYWRIGHT VERSION only — each playwright release bundles one specific
# chromium build, and the command always installs whatever build the
# installed playwright wants. So the playwright version itself is pinned in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml (both the web-ui and snapshots jobs) and recorded
# here. Bumping playwright means regenerating the baselines (see README.md)
# and updating BOTH ci.yml's pins and this file's pins, in the same commit.

playwright==1.60.0
chromium-build=1223
chromium-version=148.0.7778.96

# RULE 2 — CI-only regeneration. Baselines are produced by the CI
# `snapshots` job — `gh workflow run CI --ref <branch> -f
# update_snapshots=true` (see README.md "Regenerating baselines") — never
# committed from a local Playwright run: font rendering, the chromium build
# and antialiasing all differ from CI's pinned environment (as of #159, the
# container image mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.60.0-noble), and that
# drift silently churns the diff on the next real CI compare. (A handful of
# early Track U entries in history/ predate this rule and were generated
# locally when this repository still allowed it, with the deviation and its
# justification recorded in each entry; the rule itself does not have that
# exception going forward.)
#
# RULE 3 — history is mandatory reading, not an append target. Every
# regeneration event gets its OWN file,
# tests/web_snapshots/history/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<issue-or-track>-<slug>.md. A
# commit that changes any tests/web_snapshots/*.png must add or modify a
# history/ entry — enforced by scripts/check-snapshot-history.sh, wired into
# `make check`, so this is self-enforcing rather than a rule someone has to
# remember.
#
# Before regenerating ANYTHING, read every file in tests/web_snapshots/
# history/, in order (tests/web_snapshots/history/README.md is the index) —
# in particular:
#   - the flexbox neighbour-drift mechanism: inserting or resizing ONE
#     gallery cell re-wraps its row, so unrelated row-mates' glyphs
#     re-rasterize at a new subpixel offset and their baselines churn too
#     (issue #122) — see history/2026-09-18-106-timeline-density-aggregation.md
#     and history/2026-09-19-103-events-overflow-percentiles.md.
#   - the cross-session font-drift fix that put RULE 2's container pin in
#     place (issue #159) — history/2026-09-26-159-cross-session-drift-container-pin.md.
# Skipping that reading is exactly how a "trivial" regeneration ends up
# silently touching baselines nobody intended to change.
